   "role": "proof step",
   "reading":
   "\\forall x\\in \\mathbb{R},\\ 0<x\\Rightarrow f(x)-2=x+\\frac{1}{x}-2\\land x+\\frac{1}{x}-2=\\frac{{x}^{2}-2\\,x+1}{x}\\land \\frac{{x}^{2}-2\\,x+1}{x}=\\frac{{(x-1)}^{2}}{x}",
   "rank": 0,
   "premises": [],
   "note": "",
   "module": "Demo.Proofs",
   "meaningful":
   "∀ (x : ℝ),\n  0 < x →\n    (0 < x ∧ ¬x = 0) ∧\n      (f x - 2 = x + 1 / x - 2 → (¬x = 0 ∧ ¬x = 0) ∧ (x + 1 / x - 2 = (x ^ 2 - 2 * x + 1) / x → ¬x = 0 ∧ ¬x = 0))",
   "lean":
   "∀ (x : ℝ),\n  0 < x →\n    f x - 2 = x + 1 / x - 2 ∧ x + 1 / x - 2 = (x ^ 2 - 2 * x + 1) / x ∧ (x ^ 2 - 2 * x + 1) / x = (x - 1) ^ 2 / x",
   "justification": "Demo.Proofs.proof1",
   "index": 1,
   "cites": []},
